<title>PHILIPPINES: Philippine reserve money below ceiling.</title>
<headline>Philippine reserve money below ceiling.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-06-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Philippine reserve money in May was about 15 billion pesos below the targeted ceiling as the Central Bank maintained a prudent monetary policy, Central Bank director Diwa Gunigundo said on Thursday.</p>
<p>He said the year-on-year growth of reserve money in May was at a slow 11 percent compared with the allowable 18 percent. Growth in reserve money was at 13.3 percent for the whole of 1996.</p>
<p>The Central Bank had raised its key overnight rate since early April to support the peso and mop up excess liquidity.</p>
<p>- Manila newsroom 63 2 841-8937 fax 8176267</p>
